262
00:14:06,370 --> 00:14:08,560
No! Again, it's not the Wesley Crushers.

263
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:11,430
It's the Wesley Crushers.

264
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,860
No, if you want it to mean you're crushing Wesley,

265
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,960
it'd be the Wesley Crushers.

266
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:19,390
Do you people even hear yourselves?

267
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,060
It's not The Wesley Crushers.

268
00:14:21,070 --> 00:14:22,390
It's not The Wesley Crushers.

269
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,920
It's The Wesley Crushers.

270
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,020
Hey, look.

271
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:28,200
They named their team after me.

272
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:30,420
No, it's not the...

273
00:14:30,430 --> 00:14:32,400
Never mind.

274
00:14:34,370 --> 00:14:38,390
So, we're all clear on the bet and the stakes?

275
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:41,160
Oh, yes. The losers will be publicly humiliated

276
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:43,420
in a fashion to be chosen by the victor.

277
00:14:43,430 --> 00:14:47,290
FYI: I plan on having you publish a scientific paper

278
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:51,200
expounding the discredited Velikovsky hypothesis.

279
00:14:51,730 --> 00:14:54,530
Ouch again.

280
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:57,500
Hey, Sheldon,

281
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,660
I just wanted you to know

282
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:01,690
that I'm really looking forward to wiping the floor with you.

283
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:02,960
Oh, yes?

284
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:06,590
Well, before I respond, let me a you a question.

285
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:09,930
Is your mother a good or poor bowler?

286
00:15:16,070 --> 00:15:17,430
After you.

287
00:15:17,530 --> 00:15:18,540
No, after you...

288
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:23,670
as we are  currently crushing you, Wesley.

289
00:15:24,770 --> 00:15:30,100
It's customary for the player on the right-hand lane to bowl first.

290
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:33,400
All right.

291
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:42,860
It's a custom, not a rule.

292
00:15:42,870 --> 00:15:46,220
I so loathe you.

293
00:15:46,230 --> 00:15:48,290
That's right, Sheldon.

294
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:50,930
Embrace the dark side.

295
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:55,900
That's not even from your franchise!

296
00:15:56,470 --> 00:16:01,890
I, um, I want you to know that even though we're on opposite sides,

297
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:04,120
I, I bear you no ill will.

298
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:06,900
Thank you, Stuart. It's nice to know.

299
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:11,060
People from opposite sides often have good relationships.

300
00:16:11,070 --> 00:16:12,760
You know, Romeo and Juliet...

301
00:16:12,770 --> 00:16:15,490
Tony and Maria from West Side Story,

302
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:20,900
what's-his-name and the big blue chick in Avatar.

303
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:24,130
I'm gonna bowl now.

304
00:16:26,770 --> 00:16:28,590
Be the ball, Howard.

305
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:31,470
Leave me alone, Sheldon.

306
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:41,500
You weren't the ball.

307
00:16:42,430 --> 00:16:45,120
Hey, thanks.

308
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:46,420
This is fun, huh?

309
00:16:46,430 --> 00:16:47,720
Yeah.

310
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:49,790
It's good that we got out and did something physical.

311
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:52,290
Gets us out of our heads.

312
00:16:52,300 --> 00:16:53,190
You get in your head,

313
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,390
you start to overthink, overanalyze,obsess, you worry.

314
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:57,890
That's not what we're doing tonight.

315
00:16:57,900 --> 00:16:59,890
Tonight we're just throwing a ball at some pins.

316
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:01,320
Yeah, that's right.

317
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:05,030
and someday-- we don't know when-- maybe you'll love me back.

318
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,600
Ooh, I'm up.

319
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:14,470
Shel-don! Shel-don! Shel-don! Shel-don!

320
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:16,360
Excuse me.

321
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:21,030
I don't know who you're chanting for as I am currently the ball.

322
00:17:22,070 --> 00:17:24,520
The ball! The ball!

323
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:28,330
The ball! The ball! The ball! The ball!

324
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:33,230
Thank you, Jesus!

325
00:17:35,130 --> 00:17:37,330
As my mother would say.

326
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:44,320
I'm glad you patched things up with your boyfriend.

327
00:17:44,330 --> 00:17:46,390
Oh, yeah, me, too.

328
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,420
It's always tough when the "L" bomb gets dropped

329
00:17:48,430 --> 00:17:50,060
and you're not ready for it.

330
00:17:50,070 --> 00:17:51,520
Tell me about it.

331
00:17:51,530 --> 00:17:53,720
I dated this one girl,

332
00:17:53,730 --> 00:17:56,190
and I told her that I loved her,

333
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,560
and she said she wasn't sure.

334
00:17:58,570 --> 00:18:01,490
And she strung me along for almost two years.

335
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:02,760
It was brutal.

336
00:18:02,770 --> 00:18:04,760
Oh, I'm sorry.

337
00:18:04,770 --> 00:18:06,270
Thanks.

338
00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:09,120
I wish she had just broken up with me right there,

339
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:11,590
and put me out of my misery.

340
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,590
Really?

341
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:13,990
Yeah, would have been kinder.

342
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,290
Wil, you're up.

343
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,270
Oh, that's me.

344
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:23,790
Did you let Wil Wheaton get in your head?

345
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,060
What are you talking about?

346
00:18:25,070 --> 00:18:27,860
He's evil. He plays evil mind games.

347
00:18:27,870 --> 00:18:29,720
Did he tell you his grandmother died?

348
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:30,220
No!

349
00:18:30,230 --> 00:18:31,920
Well, if he does, don't believe it.

350
00:18:31,930 --> 00:18:34,370
He's not above playing the dead meemaw card.

351
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,660
Yes!

352
00:18:40,670 --> 00:18:43,160
Enjoy the accolades now, Wil Wheaton,

353
00:18:43,170 --> 00:18:45,290
but like your time on Star Trek: Next Generation,

354
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:49,070
your smug self-satisfaction will be short-lived.

355
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,420
Penny, you're up.

356
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:53,800
All right, remember, his meemaw's alive

357
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,060
and be the ball.

358
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:56,960
Yeah, I got it.

359
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,490
We really need a strike here.

360
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,460
I know.

361
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:01,320
So just take your time and concentrate.

362
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:02,290
Leonard, stop pressuring me.

363
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:03,360
I'm not pressuring you.

364
00:19:03,370 --> 00:19:05,260
Yeah, you are! Just back off!

365
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:08,370
Okay, I'm sorry. I'll shut up.

366
00:19:09,430 --> 00:19:11,720
I didn't mean "shut up."

367
00:19:11,730 --> 00:19:15,690
Fine. Just tell me what to do, and I'll do it.

368
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:18,520
No...

369
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:21,700
This isn't fair to you, Leonard. I'm sorry.

370
00:19:22,130 --> 00:19:23,460
Wait! Where are you going?

371
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:24,790
Penny, come back!

372
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,160
I'll get you ice cream!

373
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:28,460
No, let her go.

374
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:29,590
Are you insane?

375
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,790
If she leaves, it's over!

376
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:35,120
I'm pretty sure it's already over.

377
00:19:35,130 --> 00:19:38,200
Tough luck, Sheldon.

378
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:42,100
You did this, didn't you?

379
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:44,560
Do you think I would really break up a couple

380
00:19:44,570 --> 00:19:45,960
just to win a bowling match?

381
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:48,320
No, I suppose not.

382
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:50,700
Good. Keep thinking that.

383
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,220
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, yeah, I'm telling you,

384
00:20:03,230 --> 00:20:07,260
the Match.com chicks are much looser than on eHarmony.

385
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:11,850
You know, I-I gotta call you back.

386
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:14,800
I won a bet, and it's time to collect.

387
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,930
I don't know about you, but I feel empowered.

